{
  "slug": "impossible-materials",
  "name": "Impossible Materials",
  "description": "One product photo in: six impossible versions of your exact product — ice, jewel glass, living moss, porcelain and gold, candy, lava — each in its own cinematic world, a 4K poster of all six, and a seamless reel where the product morphs from one material into the next and loops forever.",
  "markdownDescription": "## Impossible Materials\n\nOne product photo in — six impossible versions of your exact product out, each in its own cinematic world, plus a 4K poster and a seamless morph reel that loops through every material.\n\n**Business use:** the \"what if it was made of…\" format is one of the most shared kinds of product content. Any brand — sneakers, bottles, headphones, furniture, packaging — gets six scroll-stopping posts, a print-ready poster and a looping reel from a single packshot, without a CGI studio.\n\n1. **Your product** — one clean photo, plus an optional Direction (materials, mood or palette you want).\n2. **Material Director** — reads your product and invents six materials that fight its nature (ice, jewel glass, living moss, porcelain and gold, candy, lava), each with its own colour, world, dramatic light and a physical moment caught mid-air.\n3. **Six impossible products** — rendered at 2K with your photo as the reference, so the silhouette and every seam stay yours.\n4. **The morph** — the Morph Director writes six transitions and Veo 3.1 animates each one from one material to the next, with the sound of the transformation; the last returns to the first, so the reel loops forever.\n5. **Your campaign** — Material Morph Reel (9:16, sound on) and Material Poster (4K, 4:5).\n",
  "category": "campaign-concepts",
  "outputTypes": [
    "image",
    "video"
  ],
