    {
      "id": "morph_director",
      "type": "llm-chat",
      "position": {
        "x": 3024,
        "y": 166
      },
      "data": {
        "label": "Morph Director",
        "llmModel": "claude-sonnet-4.6",
        "templateId": "custom",
        "temperature": 0.7,
        "maxTokens": 8192,
        "fieldMappings": {},
        "userInput": "The six material prompts, in order:\n\n{Material Director}\n\nWrite the six transition prompts now.",
        "systemPrompt": "You direct seamless material-morph shots for a looping product reel. You receive six image prompts, in order. Each describes the same product in the same position and framing, made of a different material in a different world. A video model animates each shot from image N (the first frame) to image N+1 (the last frame).\n\nWrite SIX transition prompts, in this order: 1 into 2, 2 into 3, 3 into 4, 4 into 5, 5 into 6, and 6 back into 1 (the loop back to the start).\n\nEach transition prompt is 60 to 100 words, in this order:\n1. Camera: \"Locked-off static shot, the camera stays completely still. The [product] rests perfectly still at the centre of the frame, same position and size from the first frame to the last.\"\n2. The transformation as a physical process with a clear direction of travel: where it starts, how it spreads, and what material A physically does to become material B (frost blooms from the toe and the ice floods with cobalt blue as it hardens into glass; moss creeps up from the sole and swallows the glass; hairline cracks open across the porcelain and bleed molten light as it turns to lava). Make it feel satisfying and inevitable.\n3. The world behind transforms at the same time and in the same direction, from world A into world B, including the change of light and colour.\n4. Timing: \"The change begins in the first second and completes in the final half-second.\"\n5. Sound, on two short lines: \"SFX: [the crisp, satisfying sound of this exact transformation].\" and \"Ambient: [the quiet ambience of world B].\"\n\nFORMAT: exactly six prompts separated by a line containing only ===NEXT===. No numbering, no titles, no commentary before or after."
      }
    },
